.TH tensor-wasm-snapshot 1  "tensor-wasm-snapshot "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-snapshot \- Save or restore an instance snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm snapshot save\fR \fB\-\-instance\fR=\fIINSTANCE\fR \fB\-\-output\fR=\fIOUTPUT\fR \fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
\fBtensor\-wasm snapshot restore\fR \fB\-\-input\fR=\fIINPUT\fR \fB\-\-as\-instance\fR=\fIAS_INSTANCE\fR \fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR [\fB\-\-max\-decompressed\fR=\fIMAX_DECOMPRESSED\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Capture or restore an instance's state to/from a \fB.tensor-wasm\fR archive via the TensorWasm HTTP API. Local\-side validation happens before any network call so the user gets a fast, clear error for the common "wrong path / unwritable output / file too big" cases without waiting on a server round\-trip.
.SS SUB-ACTIONS
.TP
\fBsave\fR
Capture the state of a running instance into a \fB.tensor-wasm\fR file via the API.
.TP
\fBrestore\fR
Restore an instance from a \fB.tensor-wasm\fR archive via the API.
.SS SAVE OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR=\fIINSTANCE\fR
Identifier of the running instance to snapshot.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR=\fIOUTPUT\fR
Output path for the resulting \fB.tensor-wasm\fR archive.
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server.
.SS RESTORE OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR=\fIINPUT\fR
Path to the \fB.tensor-wasm\fR archive to upload.
.TP
\fB\-\-as\-instance\fR=\fIAS_INSTANCE\fR
Identifier to assign to the restored instance.
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-decompressed\fR=\fIMAX_DECOMPRESSED\fR [default: 268435456]
Maximum decompressed snapshot size we will accept, in bytes (256 MiB default).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
2
Local validation failed (bad path, file too big, empty identifier).
.TP
3
Feature not yet exposed by the API (server returned 404 on the snapshot route).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1)
